  "math_index": [
    {
      "text": "<think> …, hat",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "</think>",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "<think>This image shows",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "their heads…</think>",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "<|lvr_end|>",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "<|lvr_start|>",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "<|lvr_start|>",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "<|lvr_end|>",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "<|lvr_end|>",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "vision encoder transforms the image into visual features V = vision(Xv). In parallel, the textual",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "into a representation aligned with the language model’s latent space, denoted as VT = proj(V).",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "< |lvr start| > is generated, the model enters a latent reasoning mode, where it reconstructs",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "a stopping criterion is reached. At that point, the model generate the token < |lvr end| > and",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "selects the corresponding patches and retrieves their indices I = {I1, I2, I3, . . . , ITv} from the",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "sequence of flattened visual patches in O(1) time. During the forward pass, the image is encoded",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "tokens. A subset of visual embeddings v = {v1, v2, . . . , vTv} is then gathered using the index list",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "These selected tokens are enclosed by the special tokens < |lvr start| > and < |lvr end| >,",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "t=1 that are expected to encode the underlying visual semantics. We enforce these",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "t=1 via a mean squared error",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "LLVR = 1",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "t=1",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "t=1 to answer the visual question. We adopt the standard cross-",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "LNTP = −1",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "t=1",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "log pθ(yt | y<t, h1:Tv) .",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "L = LNTP + λLVR · LLVR,",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "the < |lvr start| > token, thereby increasing the likelihood of activating the LVR process during",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "JGRPOlatent(θ) = Eq,I, o∼πθold",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "t=1",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "ri,t(θ) =",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": ", yi,<t)",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": ", yi,<t)",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "= {hlatent",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "reward, which equals 1 if the response contains both < |lvr start| > and < |lvr end| >",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "˜Ri = R(yi) −mean(R(y1), . . . , R(yG))",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "ˆAi,t = ˜Ri",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "(∀t ∈{1, . . . , |yi|}).",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "model should exit the LVR process. Specifically, when the next-token prediction introduces a <",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "|lvr start| > token, the decoder switches into the LVR mode, passing the last hidden states",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "continues producing token predictions, but it should ideally emit < |lvr end| > once an optimal",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "the distribution of the final latent reasoning token toward < |lvr end| > (close to 1), while all",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "intermediate tokens are pushed away from < |lvr end| > (close to 0). At inference time, the",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "model exits latent reasoning mode once < |lvr end| > is predicted.",
      "section_id": "sec:introduction",
      "page_start": 1,
      "page_end": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "responses per input, with a learning rate of 1×10−5, a fixed sampling temperature of τ = 0.9, and a",
      "section_id": "sec:experiment",
      "page_start": 7,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "KL coefficient of β = 0.04. This stage is applied only to the 3B variant, requiring about 20 hours to",
      "section_id": "sec:experiment",
      "page_start": 7,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "results demonstrate that incorporating a format reward based on the < |lvr start| > and",
      "section_id": "sec:method-3",
      "page_start": 9,
      "page_end": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "< |lvr end| > tokens effectively encourages the model to perform LATENT VISUAL REASON-",
      "section_id": "sec:method-3",
      "page_start": 9,
      "page_end": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "Conference on Language Modeling, 2025e. URL https://openreview.net/forum?id=",
      "section_id": "sec:references",
      "page_start": 10,
      "page_end": 15
    }
  ],
